class:: Periodicity2
summary:: Regularity of same-direction crossing intervals
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa-MS20-ESP

description::
Three outputs: periodicity, jitter, eventConfidence, each in [0,1]. Insufficient or stale history returns all zeros. Stable extra-harmonic crossings can score highly. Existing Periodicity remains a separate correlation-based analyzer.

All parameters except the signal input are construction-time numbers. Outputs are control rate. See the guide for calibration, clipping, latency and model limitations.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio input.

argument:: lowCut
Digital high-pass cutoff in Hz; zero bypasses.

argument:: highCut
Digital low-pass cutoff in Hz; zero bypasses.

argument:: threshold
Crossing threshold.

argument:: hysteresis
Schmitt half-width.

argument:: windowTime
Maximum supported history in seconds; capacity is 128 intervals.

argument:: minIntervals
Minimum complete intervals, limited to 2–64.

argument:: jitterScale
Positive reference coefficient of variation.

argument:: timeout
Stale-event timeout in seconds.

returns::
Three outputs: periodicity, jitter, eventConfidence, each in [0,1]. Insufficient or stale history returns all zeros. Stable extra-harmonic crossings can score highly. Existing Periodicity remains a separate correlation-based analyzer.

examples::
code::
{ Periodicity2.kr(SinOsc.ar(220)).poll; Silent.ar(2) }.play;
::
